WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Thanks for joining us. This is OmniView Episode 54, balanced news perspectives.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:11.620
Today is May 18th, 2026. Starting the week with a clear eye to look at the stories that matter,

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.520
Trump's warning that the clock is ticking for Iran raises risks to global oil supplies and

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.360
regional stability, as peace talks stall. US President Donald Trump posted on social media that

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.500
the clock is ticking for Iran to reach a peace deal. He warned there would not be anything left

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.020
of the country if it failed to act quickly. The statement followed extended tensions and came

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:41.600
as some regional actors' urge dialogue. Observers noted the remarks as among the most explicit from

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:48.420
the US side in recent weeks. Outlets such as the Daily Mail and Al Jazeera presented the post as a

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.160
clear escalation in pressure from Washington. They linked it to stalled negotiations and ongoing

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.780
regional incidents. The Guardian coverage framed the warning within a broader pattern of US

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:05.080
statements that combine deadlines with calls for agreement. It also noted statements from

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.800
Oman and the UAE that rejected hostile acts and called for adherence to international law.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.520
Both sides agree the talks have not produced a breakthrough. They differ on whether the language

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:22.860
strengthens leverage or narrows room for quiet diplomacy. How do public deadlines affect private

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:30.300
negotiations in high stakes conflicts? Shifting now to market reactions, major Asian indices fell

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:34.560
as investors reacted to fresh warnings from President Trump regarding Iran.

