European equity markets started the week in negative territory following the latest US statements

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:22.480
on Iran. Investors cited uncertainty over energy supplies and broader regional stability.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:29.560
Trading volumes reflected caution across major indices. CNBC reporting connected the declines to

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:35.500
ongoing concerns about the straight of hormones and possible knock-on effects for European energy costs.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:41.300
Some traders viewed the moves as a short-term repricing rather than a fundamental shift.

