00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.820
Goldman Sachs research highlighted the risk of a summer squeeze on jet fuel supplies in Europe

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:05.020
linked to the closure of the straight of hormones. A 15% reduction in flights was cited

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:10.940
as one possible market response if supplies remained tight. Airlines are already modeling different

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:16.900
scenarios. Bloomberg reporting presented the analysis as a reminder that energy route disruptions

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:23.440
can quickly affect aviation fuel availability. European carriers have begun reviewing contingency

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:29.480
