00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.660
Now, to really understand this story, there's something most coverage leaves out.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.200
Most coverage of energy route disruptions treats them as simple price spikes.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.660
Yet the mechanism involves layered logistics, contractual obligations and regulatory approvals that

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:56.360
take weeks or months to adjust. When the straight is restricted, tankers carrying crude and

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:02.220
refined products must reroute around Africa. This adds roughly two weeks of sailing time and

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:10.000
requires new port slots, insurance terms and refinery feedstock swaps. Airlines in turn rely on

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.640
forward contracts and storage inventories that were sized for normal flows. Once those buffers shrink,

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:21.900
carriers must either reduce schedules or pay spot market premiums that quickly erode margins.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.840
Knowing this, when you hear claims that airlines will simply absorb the cost,

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.980
you can check whether the carrier has disclosed hedging levels and alternative sourcing agreements

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:38.160
rather than assuming short-term resilience. Next time you see a headline about Hormuz tensions,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:44.680
ask Coo holds the physical inventory today, which refineries can process substitute crudes without

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:51.080
major retooling, and what regulatory approvals stand between a diverted cargo and an airport fuel truck.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:57.300
Ryanair's chief financial officer warned that weaker European carriers may struggle to survive a

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:03.380
