00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:09.200
should supplies tighten further. Management emphasized its own stronger balance sheet as a buffer.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:15.320
CNBC coverage presented the remarks as a signal that not all airlines are equally positioned

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:21.940
for sustained high fuel costs. Industry analysts noted that low-cost carriers with newer fleets

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:28.320
may retain an edge over older operators. Both the company and observers agree fuel represents

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:34.200
a major cost variable. They differ on how many carriers could absorb prolonged price spikes

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:40.080
without capacity cuts. What balance sheet metrics help airlines weather fuel volatility?

